ember ~0.2 s, HCFG scans 0.09 s, capstone import 0.07 s), 5-set Mastery auto-mastery-546ae191 2.6 s pinned / 1.4 s unpinned; all 23 cases pass with every answer_id filled (solver-test single 1.26 s under concurrent load).\n\n## D17 (decoder-ring) single\n- New re-asked earlier-day fields (all GM-accepted): d01 marker (.huntress string), recover_code (imm of recover_code), d02\n  mangled_score_symbol (_ZNK15DiscoveryEngine5scoreEPKc), typeinfo_symbol (_ZTI of the score class), d04 has_go_runtime,\n  d05 has_rust_mangled_symbol, d06 methods (Main-Class method-table names incl. <init>) / access_flags (class access_flags\n  decimal, 49), d07 method_count (incl. <init>/<clinit>, 7) / has_coroutine_runtime (kotlin/coroutines/ entries -> true).\n- hcfg_storage: `base64` GM-confirmed for base64-stored blobs (d08/09/11/13). RAW-stored (d12 FPC .data, d14 .hcfg section):\n  label UNRESOLVED -- `raw`, `section`, `.hcfg`-family combos, byte/array/binary/xor/blob rejected; see single_solve/HELP.md.\n\n## Proposed lib additions\n- lib/vocab.json: storage / hcfg_storage = \"base64\" for a base64 (SENGR...) stored HCFG (GM D17 d09/d08/d11/d13); \"raw\" REJECTED for raw-stored (D17 d12/d14).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D17) the \"3.31 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~4.5; harness cProfile counted ~1.1 s of imports and ~2.4 s of thread waits) -- isolated: solve.py 0.8-0.9 s wall on the 204-id single (run_solver 0.87 s; tottime is 0.24 s threaded zlib inflate of the AES members + ~0.2 s imports), 1.1 s inside the full concurrent solver-test; all 31 cases green. `hctf solver-run` wall (~6.5 s) is CLI/harness startup under load, not the solver. d12/d14 `hcfg_storage` (raw-stored) stay intentionally empty (unresolved GM label), so the single outputs 202/204.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D20) the \"5.28 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~10; the harness cProfile of the same case totals 2.2 s, mostly thread waits + imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.61 s wall unpinned, 0.61-0.74 s pinned to 1-2 CPUs on the 240-id single; in-process answer() work is 0.28 s CPU once members are decoded, unzip 0.55 s CPU (67 MB d08 inflate ~0.16 s, pycryptodome AES-CTR 25 MB ~0.1 s, sha256 ~0.04 s, all GIL-free threads); full suite passes, Mastery 0.6-2.6 s. d20_analysis_hcfg_resource_size = RS20 u32le @ magic+8 (380 on the single, matches expected).\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D21) the \"4.46 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~7-12; harness cProfile of the same case totals 1.83 s, mostly thread waits on the AES/inflate pool + 0.39 s imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.60-0.70 s wall unpinned, 0.93-1.1 s pinned to 2 CPUs on the 252-id single (252/252 match expected); no hot spot in tottime (threaded zlib inflate 0.26 s, hcfg scans 0.1 s, AES-CTR 0.09 s). Full suite 45/45 green, slowest 5-set Mastery 2.3 s inside the loaded concurrent solver-test. Nothing new to trim; the d21 loader/plugin (.cmxs) analysis adds no measurable cost.\n\nVARIANT AXIS: (speed cycle, no code change, D22) the \"3.47 s on single_solve\" flag was measured under load (load avg ~6-7.5; harness cProfile of the same case totals 1.9 s, mostly thread waits on the AES/inflate pool + imports) -- isolated: solve.py 0.60 s wall unpinned, 1.0 s pinned to 2 CPUs, 1.0-1.5 s on 1 CPU, on the 264-id single (264/264 match expected). No hot spot: hcfg() scans total 0.07 s (0.06 s is the 67 MB d08 member; the 5.7 MB bundled d22--FSharp.Core.dll scan is ~2 ms). FSharp.Core cannot be skipped: d22_artifact_sha256_3 is its sha256, and its decrypt is ~30 ms in a pool thread off the d08 critical path. Full suite 47/47 green, slowest case 2.7 s inside the loaded concurrent solver-test.\n{\n  \"65a44eb0-f8d3-41cc-886e-37afd892b23b\": {\n    \"d01_artifact_sha256_1\": \"a0d3aeddb90dccf579e0262704dc7d7c2828121d8cc988f085de169601737b9b\",\n    \"d01_analysis_elf_class\": \"ELF64\",\n    \"d01_analys