{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BSkyCwPd2N6AfLrancRKma","type":"tool_result","content":"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D22 post-run, 2026-10-22)\n\nScope: what a D23+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\nare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D22), `challenges/day22/binary-bridge-troll/solver/`,\n`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n\nProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`);\nD17 Ada ELF + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids: old days' single-solve facts re-asked on their groups + the `hcfg_storage` enum after a\nmid-day contract revision); D18 Fortran ELF (theme \"call graph / no injection\" unasked, CORRECT T+11 s). **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"\n(static-unpacking)** = ONE GnuCOBOL ELF (11 KB, `libcob.so.1`, stripped) whose HCFG is NOT in the image: a `PK19` overlay is\nappended after the section-header table (`PK19|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le len|sha256[32]|packed`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`, sha256-check,\nHCFG at out[0]). FIRST day whose prompt theme WAS asked on its own group: config_* only after unpacking + NEW `overlay_offset`\n(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\nno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n**D20 \"Resourceful\" (resources-and-overlays)** = ONE Haskell ELF (GHC 9.12.2, 1.2 MB, dynamic libgmp, not stripped) + a 463-B\n`RS20` overlay at e_shoff+e_shnum*64: `RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG resource@48 (RAW)|\nscratch` (\"private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only\"). 240 ids = 228 + 12; NEW `hcfg_resource_size` (= u32le @8, 380). The prebuilt\nRS20/question-spec unpacker + raw HCFG scan banked 239 ids at T+27 s; one field branch -> CORRECT T+49 s, 0 wrong; TT 4.8 s /\nMastery 9.3 s first try; overlay constant across variants. D19-D20 = a \"hidden storage\" arc (packed overlay -> resource overlay;\nprompt: \"resources, overlays, bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary\").\n**D21 \"Shared Custody\" (shared-library-boundaries)** = a LOADER + PLUGIN pair: `-loader.elf` (780 KB OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE,\ndebug_info, NEEDED libm/libdl/libc, Dynlink `caml_natdynlink_open`/`caml_dlopen`; NO HCFG) + `-plugin.cmxs` (9 KB ET_DYN OCaml\nnatdynlink plugin, exports `caml_plugin_header`/`caml_globals`/`camlPlugin_000*`, `Caml2007D002` dynheader, HCFG RAW in `.data`).\n252 ids = 240 + 12: `loader_machine`/`plugin_machine` (integer 62) + config_* twice (unqualified ids name the plugin IN THE\nQUESTION, plus `plugin_config_*`). The theme (exports/imports/handshake) was NOT asked. Only a routing change (question-named\nmember, applied after the qualifier peel) -> CORRECT T+1:33, 0 wrong; TT 4.2 s / Mastery 9.9 s first try.\n**D22 \"Bridge Troll\" (managed-native-bridge)** = an F# .NET 8 group of 3: `d22--sample.dll` (18.8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY, BSJB\n`v4.0.30319`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (same bytes as d03's) + `FSharp.Core.dll` (5.7 MB stock dependency, constant sha256\nacross sets). Bridge = 2 P/Invoke ImplMap rows (`getpid`@ModuleRef `libc`, `GetCurrentProcessId`@`kernel32.dll`, Winapi), trace\n`fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace`. HCFG RAW in `.text` (F# array blob) + an identical copy as a PE overlay; question: \"first\nrecord that validates\". 264 ids = 252 + 12 (3 sha256 + the d03 field family verbatim); theme NOT asked. All members silently\nrenamed `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`. Carried-over solver -> CORRECT T+47 s, 0 wrong; TT 12.3 s / Mastery (6 sets,\n1584 ids) 18.2 s first try. FIRST day re-using an old RUNTIME with a new language (.NET: C# D3 -> F# D22).\nArc since D18 = one binary-STRUCTURE concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries -> managed/\nnative bridge. Natural next (D23-D31, 9 days left): FFI on other runtimes (JNI jar+.so, Python ctypes/extension, Node N-API),\nreflection / dynamic assembly or class loading, native code carried as data, mixed-mode assemblies, more \"new language on an old\nruntime\" (VB.NET, Scala/Clojure on the JVM -- D26 leak --, Elixir, Haxe->Neko), and a backfill of the D18-D22 themes.\n**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D22); d07 `method_count` text: \"for Day 26 use the\nprimary classfile named by that unit\" (=> a JVM classfile member on D26 whose primary class is named by the question, not the\nmanifest). No new magic token in the D20-D22 contracts (D22 only reworded basenames `variant-` -> `sample`): next twist unannounced.\nLessons for D21+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- it is the layout spec; (b) every `*_size`/`*_offset`/\n`*_sha256` id maps to ONE named header field: parse the spec into a struct and expose every field; (c) grep each contract for\ntokens/days that are not today's; (d) header ids of the new member are answered by the carried-over solver; the twist is the new\nfield family; (e) `none` only for ABSENT things; (f) unguessable labels get fixed by contract revision -- re-pull; (g) D21: the\nQUESTION can name the member for an unqualified id (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member\") -- route on the text after the id peel;\n(h) D22: a group shaped like an old group inherits that group's field family; extra `.dll`s are \"delivery support only\" -- pick\nthe PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics.\nAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\nsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\nhas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\nhcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\nhcfg_resource_size, `<role>_machine` (D21 loader/plugin, integer).\nRemaining risks: (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22 (ImplMap module/import names, callconv, marshaled types, call sites) or\nan FFI bridge on another runtime (JNI, ctypes, N-API) with a native member; (1) the structure arc continues (linking internals:\nrelocations/GOT/PLT, symbol versions, RPATH/RUNPATH, TLS/IFUNC, or a PE DLL loader/plugin pair) with 2+ role members -- route by question text; (2) a backfill of the D18-D21 themes\n(call graph, PK19/RS20 header fields, NEEDED/exports/dlopen target/plugin header); (3) Neko bytecode labels (VM machine/arch);\n(4) D26 JVM classfile member; (5) per-language fact backfills (D8-D21 groups); (6) a 3+-member group (loader + several plugins,\ndecoy HCFG in the loader).\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\nllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\nrizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\nAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\njadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\nlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\nMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\nunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94af7e61-e579-412b-b282-68d4c5c3373b","uuid":"4d71cf0e-aa4f-4d99-b060-6b45d9f495f4","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:30:55.025Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D22 post-run, 2026-10-22)\n\nScope: what a D23+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\nare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D22), `challenges/day22/binary-bridge-troll/solver/`,\n`lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n\nProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`);\nD17 Ada ELF + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids: old days' single-solve facts re-asked o