{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q8Ft1QawoJxhZP9jqo2UpX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-23; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`). From Day 3 on it is CUMULATIVE: members `dNN--variant-XXX.<ext>` (`dNN--sample.<ext>` since D22), one group per\n7\t  past day, plus ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET dll, D4 static stripped Go,\n8\t  D5 static Rust, D6 Java .jar, D7 Kotlin fat .jar, D8 Swift ELF (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig (PE `.exe` in Mastery), D11 D, D12 Free\n9\t  Pascal, D13 Crystal, D14 Objective-C, D15 PAIR of C ELFs (`-stripped`/`-symbolized`), D16 PAIR of WASM (`-compact`/`-direct`),\n10\t  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + packed `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell GHC + `RS20` resource overlay, **D21 a LOADER/PLUGIN\n11\t  pair** (`-loader.elf` OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE + Dynlink, `-plugin.cmxs` OCaml natdynlink ET_DYN; HCFG RAW in the plugin),\n12\t  **D22 F# .NET** (`sample.dll` pe_cli i386 ILONLY + support members `sample.runtimeconfig.json` + `FSharp.Core.dll` 5.7 MB),\n13\t  **D23 VB.NET** (`sample.dll` 8 KB pe_cli i386 + `sample.runtimeconfig.json`; no dependency DLL).\n14\t  Since D18 each day is a binary-STRUCTURE/behaviour theme on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/\n15\t  overlays (D20), shared libraries (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), ANTI-ANALYSIS predicates (D23: \"checks the clock, sniffs\n16\t  the environment ... spot every predicate\"). D22+D23 = .NET twice in a row with a new language (C# -> F# -> VB.NET): expect more\n17\t  \"new language on an old runtime\" (Scala/Clojure/Groovy on the JVM -- leaked for D26 --, C++/CLI, Elixir/BEAM, Haxe->Neko).\n18\t  Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; a multi-member group adds a qualifier `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` (D15\n19\t  `stripped_`/`symbolized_`, D16 `compact_`/`direct_`, D21 `loader_`/`plugin_`) -- and D21 also has UNQUALIFIED ids whose\n20\t  QUESTION names the member (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member; the loader has no scored HCFG config\").\n21\t- From Day 2 on, every new-day member carries the same embedded **HCFG** config blob: `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16 len (LE) |\n22\t  u32 crc32 | xor'd JSON` (JSON at offset 12; crc32 is over the decoded plaintext). Only its storage changes (`.hcfg` section\n23\t  D2/D10/D14, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata, base64 in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW in FPC\n24\t  `.data`, WASM data segment 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D21 OCaml plugin `.data`) -- D19: NOT byte-visible (packed PK19 overlay);\n25\t  D20: RAW at +48 inside the RS20 overlay. Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND base64 `SENGR...` (crc-gate every hit); when both miss,\n26\t  look for an overlay past the ELF image and read the question text -- it spells the unpacker.\n27\t  The JSON carries never-asked keys too (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model): parse the whole dict.\n28\t- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for `exact_text` fields\n29\t  (format, machine, symbol, D17 `hcfg_storage`). **The organizers RE-ISSUE the contract mid-day** when a label is unguessable\n30\t  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> `kind: enum` + ordered rule list). Since D17 the question texts are SPECS: D19's config questions give\n31\t  the whole unpacking algorithm byte by byte. `format` is now `kind: enum` on d12-d19: `elf, pe, pe_cli, jar, wasm, neko_bytecode`.\n32\t- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19's `overlay_offset` named \"RS20 for Day 20\" (came true); still open after D22: format\n33\t  enum value `neko_bytecode` (a Neko VM member is coming) and d07 `method_count` \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by\n34\t  that unit\" (JVM classfile member on D26, primary class NOT the Main-Class). Grep every new contract for `[A-Z]{2}\\d\\d` tokens,\n35\t  `Day NN` and unseen enum values (D21, D22: nothing new; D22 only reworded basenames `variant-` -> `sample`).\n36\t- **The theme is asked on its own group only sometimes**: D5-D18 never; D19 (unpacking: `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`) and D20\n37\t  (resources: + `hcfg_resource_size`) yes; D21 (shared libs) NO -- only per-member `machine` (integer) + config; D22 (P/Invoke\n38\t  bridge) NO -- the d22 ids are a copy of the d03 family (format/machine/metadata_version/config/hcfg_version); D23 (anti-\n39\t  analysis) NO -- d22 family + `xor_key_hex`. Imports/exports/dlopen/ImplMap/predicates = backfill candidates (D17 precedent).\n40\t- **Every member since D2 embeds a \"dynamic trace\" template** (unasked): `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` {branch, event_count,\n41\t  campaign, family `<lang>_<theme>_trace`, effects, network none} gated on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (analysis/sandbox/\n42\t  workstation). family/effects: D19 `cobol_static_unpack_trace`/`memory_only_inert_payload_hash`, D20 `haskell_resource_overlay_\n43\t  trace`/`private_scratch_hash_only`, D21 `ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace`/`controlled_library_resolution_only`, D22\n44\t  `fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace`/`inert_native_process_id_bridge`, D23 `vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/\n45\t  `inert_predicate_only` (branches `success`/`decoy`/`failure`, extra field `analysis_detected`).\n46\t- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160 on D16, D17 = 204 (backfill #2: every old group padded to 11 ids), then +12/day:\n47\t  D18 216 ... D22 264, **D23 276**, no backfill D18-D23. Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies (2 sets D2-D7, 5 D8-D9, 3 D10-D14,\n48\t  5 D15-D17, 4 D18, 5 D19-D21, 6 D22, **7 on D23 = 1932 ids**); artifacts `delivery N: evidence.zip`. Timed end to end: D19-D21\n49\t  TT ~4 s / M ~10 s; D22 TT 12.3 s / M 18.2 s; D23 TT 13.0 s (solve 9.2 s under load) / M 7.9 s (solve 3.7, submit 4.1 s).\n50\t\n51\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n52\t- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n53\t  base64 in a constant pool / string literal, raw FPC `.data`, WASM data segment 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay,\n54\t  D20 RS20 overlay, D21 RAW in the OCaml plugin's `.data` (data symbol `camlPlugin_000__1`; loader: no HCFG at all), D22 RAW\n55\t  TWICE in the F# dll: in `.text` (@15891, F# static-array blob `T4022_380Bytes@`, no FieldRVA row) AND a byte-identical copy\n56\t  appended as a PE overlay past the last section (@18432 = EOF-380); question: \"accept the FIRST record that validates\"; D23\n57\t  VB.NET: RAW ONCE, only as the PE overlay right after `.reloc` (@7680 = EOF-380), no in-image copy):\n58\t  scan raw bytes for `HCFG` and `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*`, decode, accept only if crc32(plain) matches AND the JSON parses -- keep\n59\t  scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw decoys); never a fixed offset. Storage did NOT change across a day's variants on\n60\t  any day (D18 offset 8512, D19 overlay 10808/424, D20 overlay 1200888 / resource 380 in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets\n61\t  while key/campaign/crc re-rolled; D21 plugin/loader machine 62 in every set, campaign BR21-00V re-rolled).\n62\t- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- both appended exactly at the end of the section-header table\n63\t  (`e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize`), magic `<2 caps><day>`, a fixed header the QUESTION spells field by field:\n64\t  PK19 = `magic | u8 ver | u8 k1 | u8 k2 | pad | u32le packed_len @8 | sha256(unpacked) @12 | packed @44`, unpack\n65\t  `ror8(b ^ k2, 3) ^ k1`, verify sha256, HCFG at out[0]. RS20 = `magic | u8 ver(1) @4 | pad | u32le resource_len @8 | u16le\n66\t  scratch_len @12 | pad | sha256(scratch) @16 | HCFG resource @48 (raw, NOT packed) | scratch` (`private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only`,\n67\t  35 B); verify `48+res+scratch == len - o` (\"exact end bounds\") and sha256(scratch). Rule: `o = data.rfind(magic)` (\"final\"),\n68\t  read the header widths the question lists, verify bounds + hash, then the normal HCFG xor/crc/JSON at the stated offset;\n69\t  fallback for an unspecified transform = known-plaintext `HCFG` over (xor, rotate, xor). Magic for a field whose question names\n70\t  none (`overlay_size`, `hcfg_resource_size`): the `<2 caps><NN>` token whose digits = the group's day.\n71\t- **Location-as-answer** -- `hcfg_offset` (D9/D11-D14, D17-D18): base-10 FILE offset of the stored blob: base64 -> the `S` of\n72\t  `SENGR...`, RAW -> the `H`. `overlay_offset` (D19): offset of the overlay MAGIC (`P` of PK19); `overlay_size` = file length -\n73\t  that offset (header included: 424 = 44 + 380). D20 `hcfg_resource_size`: the u32le header field at magic+8 (380 = HCFG 12 +\n74\t  368 JSON), NOT the overlay size (463). Record `m.start()` of the validated hit on every scan path.\n75\t- **Storage-as-answer (`hcfg_storage`, D17, enum)** -- rules IN ORDER: `base64` if the crc-valid HCFG appears only after decoding a\n76\t  printable base64 carrier -> `raw_hcfg_section` if literal `HCFG` starts in a section named exactly `.hcfg` -> `wasm_data_segment`\n77\t  -> `raw_const_array` if in any other native data section -> else `raw`. Map offset -> section header; jars = base64. Unknown\n78\t  future token (a packed overlay is in NO section: `raw`? or a new token): read the question's rule list -- the enum is the space.\n79\t- **Any other storage encoding -> `lib.binary.hcfg_scan(data, deadline=None)`** (raw, base64 std/url/wrapped, hex, base32/85,\n80\t  UTF-16, reversed, xor'd, zlib/gzip, multibyte/rolling xor, byte maps, custom/rot13 b64, split/int-array/strided, RC4, AES/TEA/\n81\t  ChaCha, stack-built); `hcfg_find(data)` = first crc-valid + JSON-parsing hit. Kill switch `HCTF_HCFG_SCAN_EXT=0`. It does NOT\n82\t  know the PK19 rotate stub: packer overlays need their own unpack step before the scan.\n83\t- **xor key / config VALUE SHAPES** -- re-roll per variant (crc, key byte, campaign/domain/mutex/url). D23 timed modes changed the\n84\t  SHAPE, not just the digits: campaign `BRNN-00V` -> `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>` (`BR23-49B0693B`, `node-<...>.day23...`), d01\n85\t  `.huntress` marker `BR01-CATALOG-00V` -> `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `variant-000.c` -> `sample.c`. Rule: copy every value\n86\t  verbatim from the decoded bytes / symtab; never regex-validate a value shape or key on `00V` indices.\n87\t- **Container per member** -- ELF vs PE32+ `.exe` re-rolls per member in Mastery (d02 C++, d04 Go, d10 Zig PE `pe`). Labels come\n88\t  from THIS member's header. Dispatch on MAGIC, not extension: `7f454c46` ELF, `MZ` PE, `PK` jar, `\\0asm` WASM (next: `NEKO`).\n89\t  A re-asked symbol field on a PE member follows the D2 PE convention: COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>`. Extensions lie\n90\t  about the role, not the container: D21 `.cmxs` = ELF ET_DYN shared object (OCaml natdynlink plugin).\n91\t- **Member qualifier in the id (multi-member group, D15-D16)** -- `dNN_analysis_<qualifier>_<field>` names ONE member by a token of\n92\t  its FILE NAME. Rule: peel the longest field prefix that is a `[^a-z0-9]+`-separated token of exactly one member name. Tags seen:\n93\t  `stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct` (same HCFG in both), `loader`/`plugin` (D21: roles, HCFG only in the plugin).\n94\t  `sha256_K` = ARCHIVE order (central directory), never sorted.\n95\t- **Member named in the QUESTION, not the id (D21)** -- unqualified `d21_analysis_config_*` say \"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs\n96\t  member; the loader has no scored HCFG config\"; qualified ones say \"Use the unique d21-- member whose basename ends\n97\t  loader.elf\". Rule: after peeling the id qualifier, if the group still has >1 member, restrict it to the member whose basename\n98\t  ends with the token after `basename ends` / `Use the dNN--` in the question. ORDER MATTERS: run it AFTER the qualifier peel\n99\t  (running it first broke the D15/D16 qualified ids on D21: 26 ids missing from the first POST).\n100\t- **Member basename vocabulary (D22)** -- every member was RENAMED from `dNN--variant-000.<ext>` (D3-D21) to `dNN--sample.<ext>`\n101\t  (`d15--sample-stripped.elf`, `d21--sample-plugin.cmxs`, `d22--FSharp.Core.dll`) and the carried-over questions changed with it\n102\t  (\"basename starts d03--variant-\" -> \"starts d03--\"). Inner names keep `variant-000` (jar `Day06Variant000`, .NET\n103\t  `OriginalFilename variant-000.dll`). Rule: group by the `dNN--` prefix + extension/role tag only; never parse `variant-`.\n104\t- **Primary vs support members (D3, D22)** -- a managed group ships the primary assembly + `.runtimeconfig.json` (+ D22 a\n105\t  dependency DLL `FSharp.Core.dll`, sha256 constant across all sets); the question says \"Use the unique dNN-- primary managed\n106\t  assembly whose basename starts dNN-- and ends .dll; .runtimeconfig.json and dependency DLL members are delivery support only\".\n107\t  Rule: when several `.dll`s qualify, the primary = the one whose basename after `dNN--` is NOT a known framework/dependency\n108\t  name (FSharp.Core, System.*, Microsoft.*, Newtonsoft.*), equivalently the one carrying the HCFG / the `<Program>` entry point.\n109\t  `sha256_K` still covers ALL members in archive order (D22: primary, runtimeconfig, FSharp.Core).\n110\t- **Variant index per group** -- `dNN--variant-XXX` (now `sample`) re-rolls per group and mode; a carry-over d01 can re-roll STRIPPED (D15-D17\n111\t  Mastery, D17 TT) -> symbols/disassembly `[]`, has_symtab `false`, `recover_code` `none` (D17 CONFIRMED; the leaf heuristic's\n112\t  8106/8114 rejected); D18 not stripped; D19 TT and D23 Mastery set6 d01 stripped again (`none`/`false` accepted). Pair by sha256.\n113\t- **Contract wording per fetch (D17)** -- the same id's question/answer_format can change between fetches (exact_text -> enum,\n114\t  \"equivalents accepted\"). The solver reads `answer_format` per id at run time; assert enum tokens are in `accepted_values`.\n115\t- **Mastery packaging** -- `setN.` prefixed ids (2-7 sets; 7 on D23), each set its own `delivery N: evidence.zip`: pair by sha256. Each set's 1st question\n116\t  ends `Evidence case: dNN-m-<16hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha256>]` (TT `dNN-tt-...`) = set->delivery map.\n117\t- **answer_format.kind for the same field name** -- D8/D15: `elf_class`/`machine` exact_text on d01 but INTEGER (`64`/`62`) on\n118\t  d08/d15 in ONE contract. Dispatch on `kind`, not on the field name.\n119\t- **Feature-presence fields** -- `has_<thing>_section` (D10/D14 literal `.hcfg`), D17 runtime-identity booleans on old groups\n120\t  (`has_go_runtime`, `has_rust_mangled_symbol`, `has_coroutine_runtime`, `has_cpp_typeinfo/vtable`). Generic rule: `has_<x>` = a\n121\t  structural marker of <x> in THIS member; expect `has_overlay`, `has_cobol_runtime`, `has_gnat_*`-style ids next.\n122\t- **Field set per old group** -- old groups gain ids over days (D8 to 10, D17 to 11). Answer by field name from the parsed facts\n123\t  dict of THAT member; unknown field -> log and fall through.\n124\t- **Speed flags (no answer change)** -- per-case timings are usually CPU contention from parallel solver-tests: re-measure with\n125\t  `taskset -c 0,1 /usr/bin/time python3 solve.py ...`. Floor = AES-CTR+inflate+sha256 of the 67 MB d08 member (~0.35 s/set).\n126\t\n127\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n128\t| You see | First move |\n129\t|---|---|\n130\t| `evidence.zip`, \"AES Encrypted\" | `7z x -pinfected -y evidence.zip` (Python: `pyzipper`); `sha256sum *` for every `artifact_sha256_K` (K = archive order within the group) |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94af7e61-e579-412b-b282-68d4c5c3373b","uuid":"c9328837-a5c4-4579-8528-0227463c960d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:33:12.347Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# binary-reverse-engineering — technique log (days 1-23; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (OBSERVATIONS, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n- One `evidence.zip` (AES, password `infected`). From Day 3 on it is CUMULATIVE: members `dNN--variant-XXX.<ext>` (`dNN--sample.<ext>` since D22), one group per\n  past day, plus ONE new container/language per day: D1 C ELF, D2 C++ (ELF or MinGW PE32+), D3 .NET dll, D4 static stripped Go,\n  D5 static Rust, D6 Java .jar, D7 Kotlin fat .jar, D8 Swift ELF (67 MB), D9 Nim, D10 Zig (PE `.exe` in Mastery), D11 D, D12 Free\n  Pascal, D13 Crystal, D14 Objective-C, D15 PAIR of C ELFs (`-stripped`/`-symbolized`), D16 PAIR of WASM (`-compact`/`-direct`),\n  D17 Ada, D18 Fortran, D19 GnuCOBOL + packed `PK19` overlay, D20 Haskell GHC + `RS20` resource overlay, **D21 a LOADER/PLUGIN\n  pair** (`-loader.elf` OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE + Dynlink, `-plugin.cmxs` OCaml natdynlink ET_DYN; HCFG RAW in the plugin),\n  **D22 F# .NET** (`sample.dll` pe_cli i386 ILONLY + support members `sample.runtimeconfig.json` + `FSharp.Core.dll` 5.7 MB),\n  **D23 VB.NET** (`sample.dll` 8 KB pe_cli i386 + `sample.runtimeconfig.json`; no dependency DLL).\n  Since D18 each day is a binary-STRUCTURE/behaviour theme on a new language: call graph (D18), packing (D19), resources/\n  overlays (D20), shared libraries (D21), managed<->native bridge (D22), ANTI-ANALYSIS predicates (D23: \"checks the clock, sniffs\n  the environment ... spot every predicate\"). D22+D23 = .NET twice in a row with a new language (C# -> F# -> VB.NET): expect more\n  \"new language on an old runtime\" (Scala/Clojure/Groovy on the JVM -- leaked for D26 --, C++/CLI, Elixir/BEAM, Haxe->Neko).\n  Ids `dNN_artifact_sha256_K` / `dNN_analysis_<field>`; a multi-member group adds a qualifier `dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field>` (D15\n  `stripped_`/`symbolized_`, D16 `compact_`/`direct_`, D21 `loader_`/`plugin_`) -- and D21 also has UNQUALIFIED ids whose\n  QUESTION names the member (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member; the loader has no scored HCFG config\").\n- From Day 2 on, every new-day member carries the same embedded **HCFG** config blob: `'HCFG' | u8 ver | u8 xor_key | u16 len (LE) |\n  u32 crc32 | xor'd JSON` (JSON at offset 12; crc32 is over the decoded plaintext). Only its storage changes (`.hcfg` section\n  D2/D10/D14, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata, base64 in a Java/Kotlin constant pool, base64 Swift/Nim/D/Crystal literal, RAW in FPC\n  `.data`, WASM data segment 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D21 OCaml plugin `.data`) -- D19: NOT byte-visible (packed PK19 overlay);\n  D20: RAW at +48 inside the RS20 overlay. Scan raw bytes for `HCFG` AND base64 `SENGR...` (crc-gate every hit); when both miss,\n  look for an overlay past the ELF image and read the question text -- it spells the unpacker.\n  The JSON carries never-asked keys too (ipv4, windows_path, linux_path, service, host_model): parse the whole dict.\n- The analysis is easy (headers, symbols, one config blob). The hard part is the GM's exact label for `exact_text` fields\n  (format, machine, symbol, D17 `hcfg_storage`). **The organizers RE-ISSUE the contract mid-day** when a label is unguessable\n  (D17 `hcfg_storage` -> `kind: enum` + ordered rule list). Since D17 the question texts are SPECS: D19's config questions give\n  the whole unpacking algorithm byte by byte. `format` is now `kind: enum` on d12-d19: `elf, pe, pe_cli, jar, wasm, neko_bytecode`.\n- **The contract LEAKS future days**: D19's `overlay_offset` named \"RS20 for Day 20\" (came true); still open after D22: format\n  enum value `neko_bytecode` (a Neko VM member is coming) and d07 `method_count` \"for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by\n  that unit\" (JVM classfile member on D26, primary class NOT the Main-Class). Grep every new contract for `[A-Z]{2}\\d\\d` tokens,\n  `Day NN` and unseen enum values (D21, D22: nothing new; D22 only reworded basenames `variant-` -> `sample`).\n- **The theme is asked on its own group only sometimes**: D5-D18 never; D19 (unpacking: `overlay_offset`/`overlay_size`) and D20\n  (resources: + `hcfg_resource_size`) yes; D21 (shared libs) NO -- only per-member `machine` (integer) + config; D22 (P/Invoke\n  bridge) NO -- the d22 ids are a copy of the d03 family (format/machine/metadata_version/config/hcfg_version); D23 (anti-\n  analysis) NO -- d22 family + `xor_key_hex`. Imports/exports/dlopen/ImplMap/predicates = backfill candidates (D17 precedent).\n- **Every member since D2 embeds a \"dynamic trace\" template** (unasked): `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` {branch, event_count,\n  campaign, family `<lang>_<theme>_trace`, effects, network none} gated on env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (analysis/sandbox/\n  workstation). family/effects: D19 `cobol_static_unpack_trace`/`memory_only_inert_payload_hash`, D20 `haskell_resource_overlay_\n  trace`/`private_scratch_hash_only`, D21 `ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace`/`controlled_library_resolution_only`, D22\n  `fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace`/`inert_native_process_id_bridge`, D23 `vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/\n  `inert_predicate_only` (branches `success`/`decoy`/`failure`, extra field `analysis_detected`).\n- Question count: 80 on D8, +10/day to 160 on D16, D17 = 204 (backfill #2: every old group padded to 11 ids), then +12/day:\n  D18 216 ... D22 264, **D23 276**, no backfill D18-D23. Mastery = `setN.` prefixed copies (2 sets D2-D7, 5 D8-D9, 3 D10-D14,\n  5 D15-D17, 4 D18, 5 D19-D21, 6 D22, **7 on D23 = 1932 ids**); artifacts `delivery N: evidence.zip`. Timed end to end: D19-D21\n  TT ~4 s / M ~10 s; D22 TT 12.3 s / M 18.2 s; D23 TT 13.0 s (solve 9.2 s under load) / M 7.9 s (solve 3.7, submit 4.1 s).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n- **HCFG location / encoding** -- same blob, different storage per container (`.hcfg` section, .NET FieldRVA, Go/Rust rodata,\n  base64 in a constant pool / string literal, raw FPC `.data`, WASM data segment 0, Ada/Fortran `.rodata`, D19 packed overlay,\n  D20 RS20 overlay, D21 RAW in the OCaml plugin's `.data` (data symbol `camlPlugin_000__1`; loader: no HCFG at all), D22 RAW\n  TWICE in the F# dll: in `.text` (@15891, F# static-array blob `T4022_380Bytes@`, no FieldRVA row) AND a byte-identical copy\n  appended as a PE overlay past the last section (@18432 = EOF-380); question: \"accept the FIRST record that validates\"; D23\n  VB.NET: RAW ONCE, only as the PE overlay right after `.reloc` (@7680 = EOF-380), no in-image copy):\n  scan raw bytes for `HCFG` and `SENGR[A-Za-z0-9+/_-]*=*`, decode, accept only if crc32(plain) matches AND the JSON parses -- keep\n  scanning past a failing hit (D9 Nim had two raw decoys); never a fixed offset. Storage did NOT change across a day's variants on\n  any day (D18 offset 8512, D19 overlay 10808/424, D20 overlay 1200888 / resource 380 in single, TT and all 5 Mastery sets\n  while key/campaign/crc re-rolled; D21 plugin/loader machine 62 in every set, campaign BR21-00V re-rolled).\n- **Overlay layout per day (D19 PK19, D20 RS20)** -- both appended exactly at the end of the section-header table\n  (`e_shoff + e_shnum*e_shentsize`), magic `<2 caps><day>`, a fixed header the QUESTION spells field by field:\n  PK19 = `magic | u8 ver | u8 k1 | u8 k2 | pad | u32le packed_len @8 | sha256(unpacked) @12 | packed @44`, unpack\n  `ror8(b ^ k2, 3) ^ k1`, verify sha256, HCFG at out[0]. RS20 = `magic | u8 ver(1) @4 | pad | u32le resource_len @8 | u16