{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EjT4UfByn5f1XftnqwghyB","type":"tool_result","content":"      1 68:angr\n      1 131:angr\n      1 118:angr\n  {\"id\": \"member-basename-vocabulary\", \"concept\": \"Member basenames re-labelled between days (D22: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`, `sample-stripped`, `sample-plugin`) and questions reworded to match\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Group members by the `dNN--` prefix only; derive role/tag from the token after the stem (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/plugin) or from the extension; never require `variant-` or `sample`. A regression case with renamed members (sed the names in a copy of the zip listing) keeps the router honest.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. D22: no new token/day; all members silently renamed dNN--variant-000.* -> dNN--sample.* and the d03 questions dropped 'variant-' -- solvers must not key on 'variant-'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"theme-facts-recording\", \"concept\": \"Record each day's prompt-theme facts during the single solve (asked on its own day since D19, or in a later backfill)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D5-D18 themes were never asked on their own day, but D19's (overlay_offset/overlay_size, config after unpacking) and D20's (overlay_offset, hcfg_resource_size) WERE and D17 backfilled D1-D7 single-solve facts on their old groups. After CORRECT, spend <=2 min writing the theme facts (stub/overlay header fields, call graph, branch map, imports, trace family/effects, decoder) into solver/NOTES.md under `THEME FACTS dNN:`; the solver's facts dict should already expose them as candidate field names (d19: overlay_version, k1/k2 hex, packed_length, unpacked_size, unpacked_sha256). d20: rs20 version, hcfg_resource_size, scratch_size (35), scratch_sha256, scratch text, image_end, GHC version 9.12.2. d21: loader/plugin NEEDED, plugin exports (caml_plugin_header, caml_globals, camlPlugin_000__entry), Caml2007D002 dynheader unit name Plugin_000, loader dlopen/caml_natdynlink_open imports, trace family ocaml_controlled_dynlink_trace / controlled_library_resolution_only, OCaml 4.02.3. d22: ModuleRef names (libc, kernel32.dll), ImplMap rows (import name, module, MappingFlags Winapi/charset not spec), calling MethodDefs, AssemblyRefs (System.Runtime, FSharp.Core, System.Text.Json, netstandard), FSharp resources, trace family fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace / effects inert_native_process_id_bridge, HCFG .text @15891 + PE-overlay copy @18432.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"anti-analysis-gating-facts\", \"concept\": \"Anti-analysis / sandbox gating facts: environment and host-model checks, decoy branches, debugger/VM detection (TracerPid, ptrace TRACEME, CPUID hypervisor bit, DMI/VM vendor strings, rdtsc timing)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D18 had event_sandbox/event_decoy branches selected by HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL -- an 'evasion' theme is a natural next day. Facts: anti_debug (bool + technique list: ptrace_traceme, tracerpid, isdebuggerpresent, ntqueryinformationprocess, timing), anti_vm (cpuid_hypervisor, vm_strings list), env_gates [env var names compared], decoy_functions (symbols named *decoy*, or branches that skip the HCFG). MITRE T1497 / T1622. Fixtures: small gcc C ELFs with each check (static analysis only; never execute).\"},","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94af7e61-e579-412b-b282-68d4c5c3373b","uuid":"23d4b0c0-c80c-4b5b-96c7-d534ea08e0f9","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:34:07.694Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"      1 68:angr\n      1 131:angr\n      1 118:angr\n  {\"id\": \"member-basename-vocabulary\", \"concept\": \"Member basenames re-labelled between days (D22: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`, `sample-stripped`, `sample-plugin`) and questions reworded to match\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Group members by the `dNN--` prefix only; derive role/tag from the token after the stem (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/plugin) or from the extension; never require `variant-` or `sample`. A regression case with renamed members (sed the names in a copy of the zip listing) keeps the router honest.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. D22: no new token/day; all members silently renamed dNN--variant-000.* -> dNN--sample.* and the d03 questions dropped 'variant-' -- solvers must not key on 'variant-'.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"th