{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFm5hHoetsFeRoPFSZv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0185VCSBha8cSRf9shjqbaE2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; .venv/bin/python -I - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1, a[:70]\n    t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D22 post-run, 2026-10-22)\",\n    \"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D23 post-run, 2026-10-23)\")\nrep(\"Scope: what a D23+ `evidence.zip` group\",\"Scope: what a D24+ `evidence.zip` group\")\nrep(\"(lane log D1-D22), `challenges/day22/binary-bridge-troll/solver/`,\",\"(lane log D1-D23), `challenges/day23/binary-trust-issues/solver/`,\")\nrep(\"\"\"Arc since D18 = one binary-STRUCTURE concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries -> managed/\nnative bridge. Natural next (D23-D31, 9 days left): FFI on other runtimes (JNI jar+.so, Python ctypes/extension, Node N-API),\nreflection / dynamic assembly or class loading, native code carried as data, mixed-mode assemblies, more \"new language on an old\nruntime\" (VB.NET, Scala/Clojure on the JVM -- D26 leak --, Elixir, Haxe->Neko), and a backfill of the D18-D22 themes.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**D23 \"Trust Issues\" (anti-analysis-recognition)** = a VB.NET .NET 8 group of 2: `d23--sample.dll` (8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY,\n.text/.rsrc/.reloc, BSJB `v4.0.30319`, AssemblyRefs System.Runtime/Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/System.Text.Json/System.Console,\n`StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_0`8`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (d03's bytes). Predicates (theme, UNASKED):\n`Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch.StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks` (clock), `Environment.get_ProcessorCount`,\n`GetEnvironmentVariable(\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\")` vs workstation/analysis/sandbox -> branch success/decoy/failure, trace\n`vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only`, field `analysis_detected`. No ImplMap, no FieldRVA. HCFG RAW ONCE as\na PE overlay right after `.reloc` (7680 = EOF-380). 276 ids = 264 + 12 (2 sha256 + d22 family + `xor_key_hex`). Carried-over\nsolver -> CORRECT T+84 s (22 s download), 0 wrong; TT 13.0 s / Mastery 7 sets (1932 ids) 7.9 s first try. NEW in timed modes:\nvalue SHAPES re-rolled (`BR23-<8 uppercase hex>` campaign, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `sample.c`) -- harmless\nfor a verbatim-copying solver. THIRD .NET language (C# D3, F# D22, VB.NET D23) and the first BEHAVIOUR (evasion) theme.\nArc since D18 = one structure/behaviour concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries ->\nmanaged/native bridge -> anti-analysis predicates. Natural next (D24-D31, 8 days left): the rest of the evasion/obfuscation\nfamily (string encryption / managed obfuscators, anti-disassembly, control-flow flattening / opaque predicates, self-modifying\nor runtime-decrypted code, custom bytecode VM, env-keyed payloads, API hashing), crypto-constant recognition, reflection/\nruntime code generation, FFI on other runtimes (JNI, ctypes, N-API), more \"new language on an old runtime\" (Scala/Clojure/\nGroovy on the JVM -- D26 leak --, C++/CLI, Elixir, Haxe->Neko), and a backfill of the D18-D23 themes.\"\"\")\nrep(\"**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D22);\",\n    \"**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D23);\")\nrep(\"No new magic token in the D20-D22 contracts (D22 only reworded basenames `variant-` -> `sample`): next twist unannounced.\",\n    \"No new magic token in the D20-D23 contracts (D22 only reworded basenames `variant-` -> `sample`): next twist unannounced.\")\nrep(\"the PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics.\",\n    \"the PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics;\\n(i) D23: a behaviour theme (anti-analysis) on a must-not-run binary was still answered statically (header + HCFG); timed modes\\nre-shaped VALUES (`BRNN-<8hex>`) -- copy values verbatim, never validate their shape.\")\nrep(\"Remaining risks: (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22\",\n    \"Remaining risks: (00) the D23 predicates asked as fields (predicate list, env var name, compared host-model values, branch per\\nhost model, timing threshold, `analysis_detected` verdict) or an obfuscation sequel (encrypted strings/IL, anti-disassembly,\\nflattened control flow) where the HCFG is only reachable through a decoder; (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22\")\n# concept rows\nL=t.split('\\n')\ndef row(num):\n    for i,l in enumerate(L):\n        if l.startswith(f'| {num} |'): return i\n    raise KeyError(num)\ni=row(3); L[i]=\"| 3 | .NET C# / F# / VB.NET PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 (C#), D22 (F#: FSharp.Core dependency member), **D23 (VB.NET: `Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core` AssemblyRef, `StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_N`; 8 KB, HCFG RAW only as PE overlay)** -- labels identical (`pe_cli`/`i386`/`v4.0.30319`) | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over; a 4th .NET language -- C++/CLI, PowerShell-hosted, IronPython -- possible) |\"\ni=row(41); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| gap |\",\"| **seen D23 (managed form: `Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch` ElapsedTicks timing; unasked)**; native ptrace/TracerPid/rdtsc still unseen |\",1)\ni=row(80); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| gap (D18 had `event_sandbox`/`event_decoy` + host-model gate) |\",\"| **seen D23** (VB.NET: debugger + Stopwatch clock + ProcessorCount + `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` env gate -> success/decoy/failure, `analysis_detected`; theme UNASKED -- only header + HCFG ids) |\",1)\ni=row(79); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| gap (present in every member D2-D18, unasked) |\",\"| gap (present in every member D2-D23, unasked; D23 family `vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`, effects `inert_predicate_only`, + `analysis_detected`) |\",1)\ni=row(103); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| **seen D22** (all groups renamed, questions reworded; inner names keep `variant-000`) |\",\"| **seen D22** (all groups renamed, questions reworded; inner names keep `variant-000`); **D23 timed modes: VALUE shapes re-rolled too** (campaign `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, FILE symbol `sample.c`) |\",1)\ni=row(107)\nL.insert(i+1,\"| 108 | Anti-disassembly (overlapping / jump-into-middle instructions, `jz`+`jnz` same target, junk bytes after `call $+5`, fake ret, linear vs recursive sweep divergence) | gap | `objdump -d` shows `(bad)`/garbage after a branch, `eb ff`, `74 xx 75 xx`, rizin vs objdump disagree | [I] capstone recursive descent from entry/symbols; rizin `aaa`; Ghidra | med-high (evasion arc sequel to D23) |\")\nL.insert(i+2,\"| 109 | Runtime-decrypted / self-modifying code (mprotect/VirtualProtect RWX, in-place xor of a function, `.text` writable, JIT stubs) | gap | `mprotect`/`VirtualProtect` imports, W+X segment (`readelf -lW` RWE), high-entropy function body | [I] unicorn emulation of the decrypt loop; capstone on the decrypted bytes | med |\")\nL.insert(i+3,\"| 110 | Environment-keyed payload (key = hash/xor of an env value, hostname, host model, CPU count; decrypt only on the 'true' branch) | gap | decrypt routine fed by `getenv`/`GetEnvironmentVariable` result, small keyspace of compared literals | [I] enumerate the binary's OWN compared literals (workstation/analysis/sandbox) as keys, crc-gate the HCFG | med (\\\"force the truth out\\\") |\")\nL.insert(i+4,\"| 111 | Managed obfuscation runtime pieces: string decryptor (`<Module>.cctor`, xor'd char arrays, Base64+XOR), Reflection.Emit / DynamicMethod, JVM invokedynamic/StringConcatFactory, VB `CompareString` predicates | gap | `System.Reflection.Emit` TypeRefs, `ILGenerator`, a static method taking (int)->string called before every `ldstr` use | [I] dnfile + IL decoder (dotnet-il-callsite-facts), emulate the decryptor in Python | med-high |\")\nL.insert(i+5,\"| 112 | Crypto/hash constant fingerprints as answers (AES S-box, SHA-256 K, MD5 T, CRC32 table 0xedb88320, TEA delta, ChaCha sigma, FNV/djb2 seeds) | gap (decoding prebuilt) | constants in rodata/IL array blobs | [I] yara rules (findcrypt-style) over raw bytes; capstone imm scan | med |\")\nt='\\n'.join(L)\n# gaps json\nm=re.search(r'(## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n)(.*?)(\\n```)',t,re.S)\ng=json.loads(m.group(2))\nids={x['id'] for x in g}\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='anti-analysis-gating-facts']\nfor x in g:\n    if x['id']=='member-basename-vocabulary':\n        x['concept']+=\"; D23 timed modes re-shaped the VALUES too (campaign `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, FILE symbol `sample.c`)\"\n        x['detail']+=\" D23: never regex-validate a value shape (`BRNN-\\\\d{3}`) or derive anything from the `00V` index; copy decoded values verbatim.\"\n    if x['id']=='contract-forward-hints':\n        x['detail']+=\" D23: no new token/day either (Day 26 and neko_bytecode still open).\"\n    if x['id']=='theme-facts-recording':\n        x['detail']+=\" d23: VB.NET (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core, StandardModuleAttribute, VB$AnonymousType_0`8), predicates Debugger.get_IsAttached / Stopwatch.StartNew+get_ElapsedTicks / Environment.get_ProcessorCount / GetEnvironmentVariable(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) vs workstation/analysis/sandbox, branches success/decoy/failure, analysis_detected, trace vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace / inert_predicate_only, HCFG PE overlay @7680 only.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-anti-analysis-predicate-facts\",\"concept\":\"Backfill of the D23 theme on the d23 group: per anti-analysis predicate the API (Debugger.IsAttached/IsLogging, Stopwatch/DateTime.Now/Environment.TickCount64 timing, Environment.ProcessorCount/MachineName/UserName, GetEnvironmentVariable name), the compared constant (tick/ms threshold, CPU-count bound, env literal), the branch taken per HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL value, and the analysis_detected verdict\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 sample.dll (cached under challenges/day23/binary-trust-issues/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d23--sample.dll) is the fixture. Build on the prebuilt IL call-site decoder: walk Main's IL, record each call to a predicate API (MemberRef Type::Name), the following ldc.i4/ldc.i8/ldstr operand and the compare/branch opcode (bgt/blt/ceq/brtrue, VB Operators::CompareString), and the ldstr branch word each path stores (success/decoy/failure). Expose facts: predicate_count, predicates (JSON list in IL order, e.g. debugger_attached, timing, processor_count, env_host_model), env_var (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL), host_models (workstation/analysis/sandbox), branch_<model>, timing_threshold_ticks, cpu_threshold, trace_family, trace_effects. Labels unknown: prefer the API member name verbatim, decimal integers, enum tokens from the question. Never execute the sample.\"},\n {\"id\":\"static-predicate-branch-evaluator\",\"concept\":\"Evaluate env/host-model gated branches statically for ANY member (native or managed): given the predicate table, compute branch, event_count and analysis_detected for each host model without running the binary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Spot every predicate and force the truth out' = the GM can ask 'which branch does host model X take' or 'the event_count on the analysis branch'. Native: capstone over main -- getenv(\\\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\\\") then strcmp/memcmp against rodata literals, cmp/jcc to blocks that load the branch string + event_count imm. Managed: IL from the predicate-facts builder. Fall back to angr (installed) with getenv hooked to each literal, ptrace/IsDebuggerPresent hooked to 0, clock calls hooked to constant deltas; never a real run. Fixtures: gcc C ELF with 3 env branches + debugger/timing checks, and the D23 dll.\"},\n {\"id\":\"anti-disassembly-tricks\",\"concept\":\"Anti-disassembly constructs that break linear sweep: overlapping instructions, jump into the middle of an instruction (`eb ff`), jz+jnz to the same target with junk after, `call $+5; pop`, fake `ret`/`push; ret` jumps, junk bytes in .text\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Evasion arc sequel to D23 ('doesn't trust you' -> 'don't trust your disassembler'). A `disassembly`/`recover_code`-style field on a function protected this way breaks objdump linear sweep. Build a recursive-descent capstone walker (follow both jcc edges, treat opposite-condition pairs as unconditional, stop at ret/jmp) that returns the real instruction list and the leaf constant; facts has_anti_disassembly + technique list. Fixtures: gcc -c with inline asm `.byte` junk, the jz/jnz trick and an overlapping `eb ff c0` sequence; compare against rizin `pdf`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"managed-string-decryptor-emulation\",\"concept\":\"Managed string encryption: a static decryptor method (ConfuserEx-style `<Module>` method, xor'd char/byte arrays, Base64+XOR, VB Chr/ChrW arithmetic) called in place of ldstr; JVM equivalents (static String a(int), invokedynamic StringConcatFactory, ZKM-style xor tables)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the next day hides the HCFG or the predicate literals behind a managed decryptor, raw HCFG scans miss. Build: detect a method (int)->string or (byte[])->string called repeatedly, decode its IL into a tiny Python evaluator for the common ops (ldelem/xor/add/conv.u1/newobj String(char[]) / Encoding.UTF8.GetString / Convert.FromBase64String), apply it to every call site's operands, then hcfg_scan the results. JVM: same over javap -c bytecode. Fixtures: tiny C# and VB.NET programs compiled with `dotnet build` (dotnet installed) using an xor string helper; a javac class with a static xor decoder.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-anti-tamper-obfuscation\",\"concept\":\".NET protector artefacts: SuppressIldasmAttribute, renamed/unprintable metadata names, encrypted method bodies restored in <Module>.cctor (anti-tamper), invalid metadata tricks (extra #~ streams, bogus table rows), ConfusedByAttribute / Dotfuscator / .NET Reactor markers\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"dnfile tolerates most invalid metadata; ilspycmd may crash. Facts: obfuscator name (attribute/marker string), has_suppress_ildasm, renamed_types count, cctor_decrypts_bodies (method RVA bodies with high entropy / zero-length IL). The HCFG must still be found by the raw scan or after the cctor decrypt (emulate the xor loop over the method bodies). de4dot is missing (needs mono) -- note it as a tool gap; keep everything pure Python.\"},\n {\"id\":\"env-keyed-hcfg-derivation\",\"concept\":\"Environment-keyed config: the HCFG (or its xor key) is decrypted only on the 'true' branch, with a key derived from an env value / host model / hostname (xor with the literal, crc32/fnv/sha256 of it, first byte, length)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Force the truth out' suggests a payload unlockable only by the right environment. The candidate keyspace is the binary's OWN compared literals (workstation/analysis/sandbox, the env var name, campaign-like strings): for each literal try xor(literal repeated), sha256(literal)[:n], crc32(literal) bytes, fnv1a32 as key streams over high-entropy blobs near the decoder, accept only crc-valid HCFG + JSON. No external brute force. Fixtures: C ELF + C# dll that xor the HCFG with sha256(\\\"workstation\\\").\"},\n {\"id\":\"self-modifying-runtime-decrypt\",\"concept\":\"Code or data decrypted in place at runtime (mprotect/VirtualProtect to RWX, xor loop over a function body or .data, then call) -- recover statically by emulation\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: mprotect/VirtualProtect/VirtualAlloc imports, a RWE PT_LOAD or a writable .text, a high-entropy function. Build: find the decrypt loop (capstone xrefs to the protected range), emulate it with unicorn over a copy of the image mapped at its VAs (stub out the syscalls), then run hcfg_scan and the leaf-constant/disassembly extractors on the decrypted bytes. Fixtures: gcc ELF with a function xor-encrypted post-link (python patch) and an mprotect+xor stub.\"},\n {\"id\":\"custom-bytecode-vm-recovery\",\"concept\":\"Custom bytecode VM obfuscation: interpreter loop + opcode handler table + bytecode blob; the config/predicates live in the VM program\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Next step of the obfuscation family (VMProtect-lite). Cues: a big switch/jump table in a loop reading a byte pointer, a blob with low-cardinality opcode bytes, handlers that push/pop a virtual stack. Build: jumptable recovery (prebuilt) -> map each handler to a semantic (push imm, xor, add, store, jmp, cmp) by emulating each handler in unicorn on a probe state, then a Python interpreter for the blob that logs stores -> hcfg_scan the output buffer. Fixtures: a 10-opcode C VM whose program writes the HCFG bytes.\"},\n {\"id\":\"crypto-constant-fingerprint-facts\",\"concept\":\"Identify crypto/hash/checksum algorithms by their constants as answer fields (algorithm names list, constant offsets): AES S-box/Te tables, SHA-1/SHA-256/SHA-512 IVs and K, MD5 T, CRC32 0xedb88320 table, TEA/XTEA 0x9e3779b9, ChaCha 'expand 32-byte k', RC4 KSA, FNV/djb2/murmur seeds, Base64 alphabets\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"An analyst-style question ('which cipher does the decoder use') is cheap for the organizers on an obfuscation day. Build a yara/py constant table (little- and big-endian, also inside .NET array blobs and JVM constant pools) returning [(algorithm, offset, encoding)]; facts crypto_algorithms (sorted JSON), has_<alg>_constants booleans. Fixtures: tiny C programs linking each constant set; check against the existing aes-tea-chacha fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"runtime-codegen-emit-facts\",\"concept\":\"Code generated at runtime: .NET System.Reflection.Emit (DynamicMethod, ILGenerator.Emit opcode sequences, AssemblyBuilder), Expression.Compile, JVM MethodHandles/LambdaMetafactory/defineHiddenClass, native JIT buffers (mmap RWX + memcpy of an opcode array)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The emitted IL/opcodes exist only as data: recover the Emit call sequence (OpCodes.<X> field loads + operands) from the IL and rebuild the method body; for native, find the opcode byte array copied into an RWX mapping and disassemble it with capstone. Facts: has_runtime_codegen, emitted_opcodes (JSON), emitted constant. Fixtures: a C# DynamicMethod returning a constant; a C program that memcpy's `b8 imm32 c3` into mmap(PROT_EXEC).\"},\n {\"id\":\"exception-handler-control-flow\",\"concept\":\"Control flow hidden in exception/signal handling: SEH/VEH handlers, int3/ud2 + SIGTRAP/SIGILL handlers (anti-debug), C++ landing pads in .gcc_except_table, .NET try/filter/fault clauses, JVM exception tables that carry the real path\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Anti-debug classic: raise int3 and continue only in the handler when no debugger is attached. Build: parse .eh_frame/.gcc_except_table (pyelftools) call-site tables -> landing pads; PE .pdata/.xdata + VEH registrations (AddVectoredExceptionHandler); .NET method EH clauses (dnfile method body headers); JVM Code attribute exception_table. Facts: handler list with ranges, signal numbers passed to signal/sigaction. Fixtures: gcc C++ throw/catch, C with sigaction(SIGTRAP), C# try/filter.\"},\n {\"id\":\"garble-go-obfuscation\",\"concept\":\"Obfuscated Go builds (garble: hashed package/function names, -literals obfuscated strings, -tiny stripped pclntab file names) on the d04 group or a new member\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Go facts (buildinfo, function names) degrade: buildinfo may be stripped, names hashed (`Z7xk2...`), literals rebuilt by small xor/add closures at init. Build: detect garble (hashed names in pclntab, missing buildinfo deps, `-literals` closure patterns), report has_garble; recover literals by emulating the literal closures (unicorn) or by hcfg_scan over the closure immediates. Fixtures: garble needs a Go toolchain (`go install mvdan.cc/garble@latest`); if Go is absent, record as a tool gap.\"},\n]\nfor x in new: assert x['id'] not in ids, x['id']\n# insert priority-1 after the existing priority-1 block, others by priority\ng=g+new\norder={1:0,2:1,3:2}\ng=sorted(g,key=lambda x:order.get(x['priority'],3))  # stable\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+'\\n]'\nt=t[:m.start(2)]+body+t[m.end(2):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nprint(len(g))\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2380,"cache_read_input_tokens":138575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2380},"output_tokens":83,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94af7e61-e579-412b-b282-68d4c5c3373b","uuid":"863858fe-5935-47ab-85ff-4384840a7fd5","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:35:29.803Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFm59JWWaSBkdRsY1qi","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0185VCSBha8cSRf9shjqbaE2":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; .venv/bin/python -I - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md'\nt=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global t\n    assert t.count(a)==1, a[:70]\n    t=t.replace(a,b)\nrep(\"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D22 post-run, 2026-10-22)\",\n    \"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D23 post-run, 2026-10-23)\")\nrep(\"Scope: what a D23+ `evidence.zip` group\",\"Scope: what a D24+ `evidence.zip` group\")\nrep(\"(lane log D1-D22), `challenges/day22/binary-bridge-troll/solver/`,\",\"(lane log D1-D23), `challenges/day23/binary-trust-issues/solver/`,\")\nrep(\"\"\"Arc since D18 = one binary-STRUCTURE concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries -> managed/\nnative bridge. Natural next (D23-D31, 9 days left): FFI on other runtimes (JNI jar+.so, Python ctypes/extension, Node N-API),\nreflection / dynamic assembly or class loading, native code carried as data, mixed-mode assemblies, more \"new language on an old\nruntime\" (VB.NET, Scala/Clojure on the JVM -- D26 leak --, Elixir, Haxe->Neko), and a backfill of the D18-D22 themes.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"**D23 \"Trust Issues\" (anti-analysis-recognition)** = a VB.NET .NET 8 group of 2: `d23--sample.dll` (8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY,\n.text/.rsrc/.reloc, BSJB `v4.0.30319`, AssemblyRefs System.Runtime/Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/System.Text.Json/System.Console,\n`StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_0`8`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (d03's bytes). Predicates (theme, UNASKED):\n`Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch.StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks` (clock), `Environment.get_ProcessorCount`,\n`GetEnvironmentVariable(\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\")` vs workstation/analysis/sandbox -> branch success/decoy/failure, trace\n`vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only`, field `analysis_detected`. No ImplMap, no FieldRVA. HCFG RAW ONCE as\na PE overlay right after `.reloc` (7680 = EOF-380). 276 ids = 264 + 12 (2 sha256 + d22 family + `xor_key_hex`). Carried-over\nsolver -> CORRECT T+84 s (22 s download), 0 wrong; TT 13.0 s / Mastery 7 sets (1932 ids) 7.9 s first try. NEW in timed modes:\nvalue SHAPES re-rolled (`BR23-<8 uppercase hex>` campaign, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `sample.c`) -- harmless\nfor a verbatim-copying solver. THIRD .NET language (C# D3, F# D22, VB.NET D23) and the first BEHAVIOUR (evasion) theme.\nArc since D18 = one structure/behaviour concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries ->\nmanaged/native bridge -> anti-analysis predicates. Natural next (D24-D31, 8 days left): the rest of the evasion/obfuscation\nfamily (string encryption / managed obfuscators, anti-disassembly, control-flow flattening / opaque predicates, self-modifying\nor runtime-decrypted code, custom bytecode VM, env-keyed payloads, API hashing), crypto-constant recognition, reflection/\nruntime code generation, FFI on other runtimes (JNI, ctypes, N-API), more \"new language on an old runtime\" (Scala/Clojure/\nGroovy on the JVM -- D26 leak --, C++/CLI, Elixir, Haxe->Neko), and a backfill of the D18-D23 themes.\"\"\")\nrep(\"**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D22);\",\n    \"**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D23);\")\nrep(\"No new magic token in the D20-D22 contracts (D22 only reworded basenames `variant-` -> `sample`): next twist unannounced.\",\n    \"No new magic token in the D20-D23 contracts (D22 only reworded basenames `variant-` -> `sample`): next twist unannounced.\")\nrep(\"the PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics.\",\n    \"the PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics;\\n(i) D23: a behaviour theme (anti-analysis) on a must-not-run binary was still answered statically (header + HCFG); timed modes\\nre-shaped VALUES (`BRNN-<8hex>`) -- copy values verbatim, never validate their shape.\")\nrep(\"Remaining risks: (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22\",\n    \"Remaining risks: (00) the D23 predicates asked as fields (predicate list, env var name, compared host-model values, branch per\\nhost model, timing threshold, `analysis_detected` verdict) or an obfuscation sequel (encrypted strings/IL, anti-disassembly,\\nflattened control flow) where the HCFG is only reachable through a decoder; (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22\")\n# concept rows\nL=t.split('\\n')\ndef row(num):\n    for i,l in enumerate(L):\n        if l.startswith(f'| {num} |'): return i\n    raise KeyError(num)\ni=row(3); L[i]=\"| 3 | .NET C# / F# / VB.NET PE (pe_cli) | seen D3 (C#), D22 (F#: FSharp.Core dependency member), **D23 (VB.NET: `Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core` AssemblyRef, `StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_N`; 8 KB, HCFG RAW only as PE overlay)** -- labels identical (`pe_cli`/`i386`/`v4.0.30319`) | `BSJB` metadata root `v4.0.30319`, `mscoree.dll`/`_CorExeMain`, `.runtimeconfig.json` | [I] `ilspycmd f.dll`; python `dnfile` | high (carry-over; a 4th .NET language -- C++/CLI, PowerShell-hosted, IronPython -- possible) |\"\ni=row(41); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| gap |\",\"| **seen D23 (managed form: `Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch` ElapsedTicks timing; unasked)**; native ptrace/TracerPid/rdtsc still unseen |\",1)\ni=row(80); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| gap (D18 had `event_sandbox`/`event_decoy` + host-model gate) |\",\"| **seen D23** (VB.NET: debugger + Stopwatch clock + ProcessorCount + `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` env gate -> success/decoy/failure, `analysis_detected`; theme UNASKED -- only header + HCFG ids) |\",1)\ni=row(79); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| gap (present in every member D2-D18, unasked) |\",\"| gap (present in every member D2-D23, unasked; D23 family `vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`, effects `inert_predicate_only`, + `analysis_detected`) |\",1)\ni=row(103); L[i]=L[i].replace(\"| **seen D22** (all groups renamed, questions reworded; inner names keep `variant-000`) |\",\"| **seen D22** (all groups renamed, questions reworded; inner names keep `variant-000`); **D23 timed modes: VALUE shapes re-rolled too** (campaign `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, FILE symbol `sample.c`) |\",1)\ni=row(107)\nL.insert(i+1,\"| 108 | Anti-disassembly (overlapping / jump-into-middle instructions, `jz`+`jnz` same target, junk bytes after `call $+5`, fake ret, linear vs recursive sweep divergence) | gap | `objdump -d` shows `(bad)`/garbage after a branch, `eb ff`, `74 xx 75 xx`, rizin vs objdump disagree | [I] capstone recursive descent from entry/symbols; rizin `aaa`; Ghidra | med-high (evasion arc sequel to D23) |\")\nL.insert(i+2,\"| 109 | Runtime-decrypted / self-modifying code (mprotect/VirtualProtect RWX, in-place xor of a function, `.text` writable, JIT stubs) | gap | `mprotect`/`VirtualProtect` imports, W+X segment (`readelf -lW` RWE), high-entropy function body | [I] unicorn emulation of the decrypt loop; capstone on the decrypted bytes | med |\")\nL.insert(i+3,\"| 110 | Environment-keyed payload (key = hash/xor of an env value, hostname, host model, CPU count; decrypt only on the 'true' branch) | gap | decrypt routine fed by `getenv`/`GetEnvironmentVariable` result, small keyspace of compared literals | [I] enumerate the binary's OWN compared literals (workstation/analysis/sandbox) as keys, crc-gate the HCFG | med (\\\"force the truth out\\\") |\")\nL.insert(i+4,\"| 111 | Managed obfuscation runtime pieces: string decryptor (`<Module>.cctor`, xor'd char arrays, Base64+XOR), Reflection.Emit / DynamicMethod, JVM invokedynamic/StringConcatFactory, VB `CompareString` predicates | gap | `System.Reflection.Emit` TypeRefs, `ILGenerator`, a static method taking (int)->string called before every `ldstr` use | [I] dnfile + IL decoder (dotnet-il-callsite-facts), emulate the decryptor in Python | med-high |\")\nL.insert(i+5,\"| 112 | Crypto/hash constant fingerprints as answers (AES S-box, SHA-256 K, MD5 T, CRC32 table 0xedb88320, TEA delta, ChaCha sigma, FNV/djb2 seeds) | gap (decoding prebuilt) | constants in rodata/IL array blobs | [I] yara rules (findcrypt-style) over raw bytes; capstone imm scan | med |\")\nt='\\n'.join(L)\n# gaps json\nm=re.search(r'(## Readiness gaps\\n```json\\n)(.*?)(\\n```)',t,re.S)\ng=json.loads(m.group(2))\nids={x['id'] for x in g}\ng=[x for x in g if x['id']!='anti-analysis-gating-facts']\nfor x in g:\n    if x['id']=='member-basename-vocabulary':\n        x['concept']+=\"; D23 timed modes re-shaped the VALUES too (campaign `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, FILE symbol `sample.c`)\"\n        x['detail']+=\" D23: never regex-validate a value shape (`BRNN-\\\\d{3}`) or derive anything from the `00V` index; copy decoded values verbatim.\"\n    if x['id']=='contract-forward-hints':\n        x['detail']+=\" D23: no new token/day either (Day 26 and neko_bytecode still open).\"\n    if x['id']=='theme-facts-recording':\n        x['detail']+=\" d23: VB.NET (Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core, StandardModuleAttribute, VB$AnonymousType_0`8), predicates Debugger.get_IsAttached / Stopwatch.StartNew+get_ElapsedTicks / Environment.get_ProcessorCount / GetEnvironmentVariable(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) vs workstation/analysis/sandbox, branches success/decoy/failure, analysis_detected, trace vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace / inert_predicate_only, HCFG PE overlay @7680 only.\"\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-anti-analysis-predicate-facts\",\"concept\":\"Backfill of the D23 theme on the d23 group: per anti-analysis predicate the API (Debugger.IsAttached/IsLogging, Stopwatch/DateTime.Now/Environment.TickCount64 timing, Environment.ProcessorCount/MachineName/UserName, GetEnvironmentVariable name), the compared constant (tick/ms threshold, CPU-count bound, env literal), the branch taken per HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL value, and the analysis_detected verdict\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D23 sample.dll (cached under challenges/day23/binary-trust-issues/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d23--sample.dll) is the fixture. Build on the prebuilt IL call-site decoder: walk Main's IL, record each call to a predicate API (MemberRef Type::Name), the following ldc.i4/ldc.i8/ldstr operand and the compare/branch opcode (bgt/blt/ceq/brtrue, VB Operators::CompareString), and the ldstr branch word each path stores (success/decoy/failure). Expose facts: predicate_count, predicates (JSON list in IL order, e.g. debugger_attached, timing, processor_count, env_host_model), env_var (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL), host_models (workstation/analysis/sandbox), branch_<model>, timing_threshold_ticks, cpu_threshold, trace_family, trace_effects. Labels unknown: prefer the API member name verbatim, decimal integers, enum tokens from the question. Never execute the sample.\"},\n {\"id\":\"static-predicate-branch-evaluator\",\"concept\":\"Evaluate env/host-model gated branches statically for ANY member (native or managed): given the predicate table, compute branch, event_count and analysis_detected for each host model without running the binary\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Spot every predicate and force the truth out' = the GM can ask 'which branch does host model X take' or 'the event_count on the analysis branch'. Native: capstone over main -- getenv(\\\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\\\") then strcmp/memcmp against rodata literals, cmp/jcc to blocks that load the branch string + event_count imm. Managed: IL from the predicate-facts builder. Fall back to angr (installed) with getenv hooked to each literal, ptrace/IsDebuggerPresent hooked to 0, clock calls hooked to constant deltas; never a real run. Fixtures: gcc C ELF with 3 env branches + debugger/timing checks, and the D23 dll.\"},\n {\"id\":\"anti-disassembly-tricks\",\"concept\":\"Anti-disassembly constructs that break linear sweep: overlapping instructions, jump into the middle of an instruction (`eb ff`), jz+jnz to the same target with junk after, `call $+5; pop`, fake `ret`/`push; ret` jumps, junk bytes in .text\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Evasion arc sequel to D23 ('doesn't trust you' -> 'don't trust your disassembler'). A `disassembly`/`recover_code`-style field on a function protected this way breaks objdump linear sweep. Build a recursive-descent capstone walker (follow both jcc edges, treat opposite-condition pairs as unconditional, stop at ret/jmp) that returns the real instruction list and the leaf constant; facts has_anti_disassembly + technique list. Fixtures: gcc -c with inline asm `.byte` junk, the jz/jnz trick and an overlapping `eb ff c0` sequence; compare against rizin `pdf`.\"},\n {\"id\":\"managed-string-decryptor-emulation\",\"concept\":\"Managed string encryption: a static decryptor method (ConfuserEx-style `<Module>` method, xor'd char/byte arrays, Base64+XOR, VB Chr/ChrW arithmetic) called in place of ldstr; JVM equivalents (static String a(int), invokedynamic StringConcatFactory, ZKM-style xor tables)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the next day hides the HCFG or the predicate literals behind a managed decryptor, raw HCFG scans miss. Build: detect a method (int)->string or (byte[])->string called repeatedly, decode its IL into a tiny Python evaluator for the common ops (ldelem/xor/add/conv.u1/newobj String(char[]) / Encoding.UTF8.GetString / Convert.FromBase64String), apply it to every call site's operands, then hcfg_scan the results. JVM: same over javap -c bytecode. Fixtures: tiny C# and VB.NET programs compiled with `dotnet build` (dotnet installed) using an xor string helper; a javac class with a static xor decoder.\"},\n {\"id\":\"dotnet-anti-tamper-obfuscation\",\"concept\":\".NET protector artefacts: SuppressIldasmAttribute, renamed/unprintable metadata names, encrypted method bodies restored in <Module>.cctor (anti-tamper), invalid metadata tricks (extra #~ streams, bogus table rows), ConfusedByAttribute / Dotfuscator / .NET Reactor markers\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"dnfile tolerates most invalid metadata; ilspycmd may crash. Facts: obfuscator name (attribute/marker string), has_suppress_ildasm, renamed_types count, cctor_decrypts_bodies (method RVA bodies with high entropy / zero-length IL). The HCFG must still be found by the raw scan or after the cctor decrypt (emulate the xor loop over the method bodies). de4dot is missing (needs mono) -- note it as a tool gap; keep everything pure Python.\"},\n {\"id\":\"env-keyed-hcfg-derivation\",\"concept\":\"Environment-keyed config: the HCFG (or its xor key) is decrypted only on the 'true' branch, with a key derived from an env value / host model / hostname (xor with the literal, crc32/fnv/sha256 of it, first byte, length)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"'Force the truth out' suggests a payload unlockable only by the right environment. The candidate keyspace is the binary's OWN compared literals (workstation/analysis/sandbox, the env var name, campaign-like strings): for each literal try xor(literal repeated), sha256(literal)[:n], crc32(literal) bytes, fnv1a32 as key streams over high-entropy blobs near the decoder, accept only crc-valid HCFG + JSON. No external brute force. Fixtures: C ELF + C# dll that xor the HCFG with sha256(\\\"workstation\\\").\"},\n {\"id\":\"self-modifying-runtime-decrypt\",\"concept\":\"Code or data decrypted in place at runtime (mprotect/VirtualProtect to RWX, xor loop over a function body or .data, then call) -- recover statically by emulation\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Cues: mprotect/VirtualProtect/VirtualAlloc imports, a RWE PT_LOAD or a writable .text, a high-entropy function. Build: find the decrypt loop (capstone xrefs to the protected range), emulate it with unicorn over a copy of the image mapped at its VAs (stub out the syscalls), then run hcfg_scan and the leaf-constant/disassembly extractors on the decrypted bytes. Fixtures: gcc ELF with a function xor-encrypted post-link (python patch) and an mprotect+xor stub.\"},\n {\"id\":\"custom-bytecode-vm-recovery\",\"concept\":\"Custom bytecode VM obfuscation: interpreter loop + opcode handler table + bytecode blob; the config/predicates live in the VM program\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Next step of the obfuscation family (VMProtect-lite). Cues: a big switch/jump table in a loop reading a byte pointer, a blob with low-cardinality opcode bytes, handlers that push/pop a virtual stack. Build: jumptable recovery (prebuilt) -> map each handler to a semantic (push imm, xor, add, store, jmp, cmp) by emulating each handler in unicorn on a probe state, then a Python interpreter for the blob that logs stores -> hcfg_scan the output buffer. Fixtures: a 10-opcode C VM whose program writes the HCFG bytes.\"},\n {\"id\":\"crypto-constant-fingerprint-facts\",\"concept\":\"Identify crypto/hash/checksum algorithms by their constants as answer fields (algorithm names list, constant offsets): AES S-box/Te tables, SHA-1/SHA-256/SHA-512 IVs and K, MD5 T, CRC32 0xedb88320 table, TEA/XTEA 0x9e3779b9, ChaCha 'expand 32-byte k', RC4 KSA, FNV/djb2/murmur seeds, Base64 alphabets\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"An analyst-style question ('which cipher does the decoder use') is cheap for the organizers on an obfuscation day. Build a yara/py constant table (little- and big-endian, also inside .NET array blobs and JVM constant pools) returning [(algorithm, offset, encoding)]; facts crypto_algorithms (sorted JSON), has_<alg>_constants booleans. Fixtures: tiny C programs linking each constant set; check against the existing aes-tea-chacha fixtures.\"},\n {\"id\":\"runtime-codegen-emit-facts\",\"concept\":\"Code generated at runtime: .NET System.Reflection.Emit (DynamicMethod, ILGenerator.Emit opcode sequences, AssemblyBuilder), Expression.Compile, JVM MethodHandles/LambdaMetafactory/defineHiddenClass, native JIT buffers (mmap RWX + memcpy of an opcode array)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"The emitted IL/opcodes exist only as data: recover the Emit call sequence (OpCodes.<X> field loads + operands) from the IL and rebuild the method body; for native, find the opcode byte array copied into an RWX mapping and disassemble it with capstone. Facts: has_runtime_codegen, emitted_opcodes (JSON), emitted constant. Fixtures: a C# DynamicMethod returning a constant; a C program that memcpy's `b8 imm32 c3` into mmap(PROT_EXEC).\"},\n {\"id\":\"exception-handler-control-flow\",\"concept\":\"Control flow hidden in exception/signal handling: SEH/VEH handlers, int3/ud2 + SIGTRAP/SIGILL handlers (anti-debug), C++ landing pads in .gcc_except_table, .NET try/filter/fault clauses, JVM exception tables that carry the real path\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Anti-debug classic: raise int3 and continue only in the handler when no debugger is attached. Build: parse .eh_frame/.gcc_except_table (pyelftools) call-site tables -> landing pads; PE .pdata/.xdata + VEH registrations (AddVectoredExceptionHandler); .NET method EH clauses (dnfile method body headers); JVM Code attribute exception_table. Facts: handler list with ranges, signal numbers passed to signal/sigaction. Fixtures: gcc C++ throw/catch, C with sigaction(SIGTRAP), C# try/filter.\"},\n {\"id\":\"garble-go-obfuscation\",\"concept\":\"Obfuscated Go builds (garble: hashed package/function names, -literals obfuscated strings, -tiny stripped pclntab file names) on the d04 group or a new member\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Go facts (buildinfo, function names) degrade: buildinfo may be stripped, names hashed (`Z7xk2...`), literals rebuilt by small xor/add closures at init. Build: detect garble (hashed names in pclntab, missing buildinfo deps, `-literals` closure patterns), report has_garble; recover literals by emulating the literal closures (unicorn) or by hcfg_scan over the closure immediates. Fixtures: garble needs a Go toolchain (`go install mvdan.cc/garble@latest`); if Go is absent, record as a tool gap.\"},\n]\nfor x in new: assert x['id'] not in ids, x['id']\n# insert priority-1 after the existing priority-1 block, others by priority\ng=g+new\norder={1:0,2:1,3:2}\ng=sorted(g,key=lambda x:order.get(x['priority'],3))  # stable\nbody='[\\n'+',\\n'.join('  '+json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False) for x in g)+'\\n]'\nt=t[:m.start(2)]+body+t[m.end(2):]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nprint(len(g))\nEOF"}}}
